British actor Ray Panthaki &#x2013; known for &#x201C;Boiling Point&#x201D; and &#x201C;Marcella&#x201D; &#x2013; goes personal in directorial debut &#x201C; In Starland .&#x201D; Very personal.

&#x201C;I was a young carer and often felt I hadn&#x2019;t come of age when society tells you that you&#x2019;re supposed to. I had responsibilities that most people my age didn&#x2019;t. That changed when my acting career took off in my early twenties, but I&#x2019;d carried this thought around: what if someone got to their forties and had never really lived? I found that quite heartbreaking, but also full of possibility.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Judge Dismisses Trump’s Wall Street Journal Defamation Lawsuit Over Published Epstein ‘Birthday Book’ for a Second Time Amid Flight Halt, Trump Meets With Jon Voight to Talk U.S. Film Incentive: 'Get This Done!'

He adds: &#x201C;It might never be too late to become the person you were supposed to be.&#x201D;

Ernie ( Clarence Maclin ) is about to discover this when his quiet, unremarkable life in a small American town is turned upside down by a group of young influencers who force him out of his shell. Panthaki describes his film as a &#x201C;coming-of-middle-age story.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I don&#x2019;t believe that becoming yourself is something reserved for the young. Sometimes it takes half a lifetime to understand what&#x2019;s been holding you back, and perhaps another half to do something about it.&#x201D;

His characters keep on fighting: for companionship &#x2013; like Ernie &#x2013; or for internet fame and glory like some of his new friends. What unites them is loneliness.

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s something I&#x2019;ve experienced myself, and I&#x2019;ve seen people very close to me go through it. Particularly with older people, there&#x2019;s something about someone having lived this entire life and then finding themselves alone that I find incredibly moving. It wasn&#x2019;t really a question of whether I&#x2019;d explore it, but when,&#x201D; notes Panthaki. He calls loneliness &#x201C;one of the great contradictions of our time.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;We&#x2019;ve never been more connected, and yet we seem to be feeling more disconnected than ever.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I suppose that&#x2019;s where the film becomes quite spiritual for me. Beneath all the noise, the technology and performance, we&#x2019;re all just human beings looking for love, acceptance and a sense of belonging. There&#x2019;s a big difference between being seen and being known. Maybe that&#x2019;s what the film is really about.&#x201D;

Panthaki has a &#x201C;huge amount of hope&#x201D; in the new generation, but also admits they&#x2019;ve inherited a world where everything is &#x201C;increasingly measured in numbers.&#x201D;

&#x201C;The irony is that at one point I tried to play that game myself. We&#x2019;d spent years trying to finance the film, and I thought: Right. If the industry wants numbers, I&#x2019;ll give them numbers. I&#x2019;ll cast ten influencers with a combined following of 250 million people. Except I wasn&#x2019;t particularly comfortable with it,&#x201D; he recalls.

He changed his mind, ultimately choosing people who were simply right for the part.

&#x201C;No follower counts, no industry heat, no looking at what people had done before,&#x201D; he says.

&#x201C;As an actor, I know what it feels like to be judged on things that have nothing to do with your ability to do the job. I know what it&#x2019;s like to lose a job when everyone wants you, but the studio wants a bigger name. There was something quite satisfying to finally be in a position to correct some of the things I&#x2019;d experienced myself.&#x201D;

&#x201C;On the first day of rehearsals, I told the cast that we were going to make this film for every single &#x2018;no&#x2019; we&#x2019;d ever had as artists.&#x201D;

For the role of Ernie, Panthaki was looking for someone &#x201C;who could communicate an entire lifetime without saying very much.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Clarence has this extraordinary quality where you can just stay on his face and feel the weight of everything that&#x2019;s happened to him. There&#x2019;s a tremendous vulnerability there, but also something unpredictable and even dangerous,&#x201D; he says.

&#x201C;He wasn&#x2019;t the Ernie I&#x2019;d imagined when we wrote the script. But there was something in his screen test that I couldn&#x2019;t ignore &#x2013; a truth that would be very difficult to manufacture.&#x201D;

It wasn&#x2019;t easy to get &#x201C;In Starland&#x201D; off the ground.

Produced by Le Bateau Lavoir, Archface Films and Killer Films, it world-premieres at Tallinn Black Nights Film Festival . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I got to make the film I wanted to make, with the people I wanted to make it with, without having to compromise my beliefs. It&#x2019;s the hardest thing I&#x2019;ve ever done, but it feels quite fitting to have spent seven years making a film about a man who&#x2019;s trying to find his own way in the world.&#x201D;

He doesn&#x2019;t like to call it an indie, however.

&#x201C;There are films that are considered independent that still have a whole infrastructure of public funding and institutional support behind them. We didn&#x2019;t have any of that. I&#x2019;ve embraced the term &#x2018; non-dependent&#x2019; , which Ted Hope has written about,&#x201D; he says.

&#x201C;So many things that happened throughout this process that I couldn&#x2019;t have planned or explained. They only strengthened my belief that this was a story I was meant to tell, and that there was a reason it needed to be told now.&#x201D;

Panthaki also ignored the naysayers also when completing the soundtrack. Obsessed with '80s hits, he made sure his characters loved them too.

&#x201C;Nothing like disguising your own taste in music as character development! Nostalgia is such a powerful thing. Music can take you back 40 years in a second, and I wanted the audience to feel that. Particularly through Ernie, who&#x2019;s carrying around a whole lifetime of memories and experiences,&#x201D; he says. He wrote all the songs into the script.

&#x201C;I knew exactly what I wanted and where I wanted it, but getting them was a different story. &#x2018;Everybody Wants to Rule the World&#x2019; is one of the greatest songs ever written. It captured so much of what the film was exploring. Power, control, celebrity, and this very human desire to feel important. I couldn&#x2019;t imagine opening the film any other way.&#x201D;

He wrote to some of the musicians personally.

&#x201C;We had absolutely no business trying to get [these songs] on our budget, but I&#x2019;ve always believed in going directly to artists. You&#x2019;d be surprised how often people want to help when they understand your &#x2018;why&#x2019;,&#x201D; he recalls.

&#x201C;I&#x2019;ve spent seven years being told we couldn&#x2019;t do things. We couldn&#x2019;t shoot in America on that budget; we couldn&#x2019;t make it in 20 days; we couldn&#x2019;t get those actors; we couldn&#x2019;t afford that music. And we just kept finding ways.&#x201D;

&#x201C;There&#x2019;s very little in this film that we haven&#x2019;t had to fight for in some way.&#x201D;

