A Google spokesperson said: "We&#x2019;re aware of the new content and our teams are investigating. We suspended Russell Brand&#x2019;s channel from the YouTube Partner Program in September 2023. The channel has not been able to monetise on YouTube since then."

Reading from a notepad, Laura Brand told Russell Brand's followers: &#x201C;Beloved brothers and sisters in Christ, God bless you for your support. As you know, I am not guilty for the offences I have been jailed for, so something strange is happening.&#x201D;

She continued: &#x201C;The good news is that Christ is with us when we choose him, and I do. I am incarcerated in HMP Littlehey. Little as in small, and hey as in, &#x2018;Hey, I&#x2019;m in the biggest sex offenders&#x2019; prison in Europe.

&#x201C;The good news is that I have already seen that the staff here are strong, they are kind, and they are dedicated. And as for my fellow prisoners, I now know that I am in no position to judge anyone.

&#x201C;I don&#x2019;t know which other men here are not guilty, and the ones that are, they are people that Christ died to save, like you and me. Let us all love, pray for, and forgive one another as God forgave us.&#x201D;

An audibly emotional Laura Brand added: &#x201C;Please support my treasured wife and family. I feel your prayers, your brother in Christ. Russell.&#x201D;

EXCLUSIVE: Author Yomi Adegoke ( The List ) has penned Playing The Game, a new audio series launching on Audible on December 3.

The series is described as a &#x201C;satirical romantic comedy set on Britain&#x2019;s biggest dating show where the aim is to find love, but the plan is to fake.&#x201D;

Playing The Game stars Aim&#xE9;e Kelly ( Forever Home ) and Jon Pointing ( Big Boys ) as the leads, joined by Lucy Punch ( Amandaland ), Zeze Millz ( Do Not Disturb ), Charithra Chandran ( Bridgerton ), and Paddy Young ( Saturday Night Live UK ). Related Stories News Sue Perkins Exploring ADHD Diagnosis For First Time In Audible Podcast 'Attention, Please! Tales From A Distracted Mind' News 'Grey Gardens' Helmer Michael Sucsy Sets Audible Adaptation 'A Murder To Remember' With Amazon MGM Studios

